{"agent":"lane6-kilo","data":{"budget":"","claim":"ddflow/api/cirun.py:_keep_failing_ids records only failing_ids_note and does not write the failing_ids blob when a non-test check fails beside red tests, so gate_baseline._ci_ids cannot recover the ids and the red tests are never measured on the base","falsifier":"a direct call of _keep_failing_ids with a Result failing 'ruff check' plus red tests returns a dict WITHOUT a failing_ids key (only failing_ids_note)","item":"fix-Ba17fabe249","mechanism":"the 'if not BL.only_tests_failed(res.checks)' branch stores a 'not kept' note instead of the blob that BL.read_full reads back","probe":"python call constructing Result(status=failed, checks=[Check('ruff check',False), Check('unit tests + end-to-end scenarios',False)], failures={'failed_tests':['tests/test_x.py::test_a']}); then BL.read_full on the returned blob","probe_output":"after the fix it returns failing_ids and read_full recovers ['tests/test_x.py::test_a']; before the fix it returned only failing_ids_note","question":"Does a ci run that fails with BOTH a non-test check and red tests keep the failing test ids aside, so the baseline of those tests can be measured on the base?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e633037760074c558e11ebc69","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":168010,"schema":1,"subject":"R4ffaaa760f","ts":"2026-11-10T22:24:27.959790Z"}
